 ## Unreleased
 
+- `bin/aic notes:stats` prints how many notes and users the app holds.
+
 ### Added
 
 - **The guard judges a write by where it really lands** (#125). Found in #118's proof, where an agent followed a symlinked `vendor/ignibyte/aic-*` into AIC's own repository. Every write the guard sees (an edit, an MCP tool's path, a shell redirect, `cp`, `tee`, `sed -i`) is resolved to its real path, through the deepest existing folder for a new file, and refused at every enforcement level, run or no run, when it lands outside the project or under `vendor/`. Only `/dev/` stays open, so `2>/dev/null` still works. Proved in a scratch app whose `vendor/ignibyte/aic-framework` links back to this repository.
